    "enrich_notes": "Treatment volume is tied to Vol I §8.3/§9 efficiency, not a fixed WQv depth in this excerpt. Retention and exfiltration recovery is 72 h at average AMC; exfiltration may use SF=2 (half infiltration rate or 36 h drawdown). Wet detention draws down half the treatment volume in 48–60 h; permanent pool sized for 21-day residence (wet-season rainfall). Exfiltration trench invert ≥2 ft above seasonal high GW; min 3 ft trench width, 2 in min pipe ID. Swales: HSG A/B, 3-year 1-hour storm infiltration, cross-section top width:depth ≥6:1 or side slopes ≤3:1 H:V. Wet pond max depth 12 ft; L:W ≥2:1. Base flow: storage volumes exclude volume below seasonal high water table (no minimum separation inches for ponds in excerpt).",
